Consider the following CSS and HTML structure:
html
<div class="container">
  <p>This is some <span>important</span> text.</p>
  <a href="#">Click me</a>
</div>

css
.container {
  color: red;
}
p {
  color: blue;
  background-color: lightgray;
}
span {
  color: green;
}
a {
  color: purple;
  text-decoration: none;
}

What will be the final computed color of the word "important" and the hyperlink text "Click me", respectively?

Consider the following HTML and CSS:
html
<div id="main-content" class="container">
  <p class="text-primary">Hello <span>world</span>!</p>
</div>

css
#main-content p {
  color: red; /* Rule 1 */
}
.container .text-primary {
  color: blue; /* Rule 2 */
}
p.text-primary {
  color: green; /* Rule 3 */
}

What will be the final computed color of the text "Hello world!"?

